  "sport": "floorball",
  "title": "The chain – two handovers and a free finish",
  "description": "One goal with a goalkeeper and three lines just inside the centre line: A by the left board, C in the middle and B by the right board. The balls are with C. C carries the ball diagonally forward to the left and hands it over to A, who comes in behind. A carries it diagonally forward to the right and hands it over to B, who also comes in behind. A and C carry on towards a post each, and B chooses to shoot or to pass to A or C for a first-time shot.\n\nSwitch lines after each turn: A to B, B to C and C to A. Run it just as much mirrored. The diagram is not to scale.",
  "coachingPoints": [
    {
      "id": "cp1",
      "text": "The player taking over the ball always comes in behind the ball carrier."
    },
    {
      "id": "cp2",
      "text": "Leave the ball dead at the handover – the receiver takes it at speed."
    },
    {
      "id": "cp3",
      "text": "B: read the situation and choose – shoot, or pass to whoever is most open."
    },
    {
      "id": "cp4",
      "text": "Everyone follows up on goal for the rebounds."
    }
  ],
